diff --git a/docs/subsystems/providers-accounts.md b/docs/subsystems/providers-accounts.md
index 01fe8f728cfa1837b262dd9fafcf0731198e2d5f..dc833d468840aec0fab5248b89988767149a1af8 100644
--- a/docs/subsystems/providers-accounts.md
+++ b/docs/subsystems/providers-accounts.md
@@ -1,5 +1,21 @@
 # Providers and accounts
 
+The desktop Providers page can preview a local WorkBuddy or CodeBuddy JSON
+export for both regions. Preview never writes credentials or refreshes tokens.
+The default transfer mode requires a usable refresh credential and uses the
+plugin's ImportFiles hook to validate, rotate and save it, as a browser sign-in
+does. Existing access-only sign-ins can be upgraded in this mode. The source
+device may need to sign in again after its refresh credential is rotated.
+With transfer off, only a currently valid access token is saved, and an
+existing provider/UID is kept under the host's auth lock. Expired access-only
+credentials require a fresh sign-in. See
+[`workbuddy_import.go`](../../internal/gui/workbuddy_import.go) and
+[`ImportNewUID`](../../internal/plugin/providers.go).
+The desktop export lists local WorkBuddy sign-ins and saves the selected
+accounts to a native folder picker destination. The JSON remains compatible
+with the mobile importer. See
+[`workbuddy_export.go`](../../internal/gui/workbuddy_export.go).
+
 The gateway can send a request to three kinds of upstream:
 
 - A **provider** in `providers.json`: an endpoint with one or more API keys. Google Vertex AI's is signed with the user's Google credentials, or with one API key (express mode).
